      "preprocessing": "Unscoped candidate rows. Approve the full-key population at cutover; use customer-cohort-project.json. Customers and suppliers require Business Partner/CVI mapping, roles and numbering. FI BSEG may be a cluster table in ECC and therefore cannot be assumed readable by CDS; use the full-row ABAP helper or a verified extraction interface when necessary. Open-at-cutover means posted by cutover and not cleared by cutover, including subsequently cleared items. Separate currencies, debit/credit signs, ledgers and fiscal periods; prevent double-counting subledger openings in G/L balances. Choose classic OR new G/L for each ledger population; do not union both. DDIC must confirm all ledger dimensions and include any additional keys. Period 00 is carryforward, not period 01; calculate cutoff totals from the approved fiscal-year/period contract, including special periods only as intended. Enrich currency types from ledger/company configuration and classify accounts from SKB1. Exclude balances already supplied by FI-AA/AP/AR/open-item migration; reconcile migration clearing accounts to zero. No automatic totals-to-posting transformation is supplied."
